.TH MU2EDAQ\-DISCOVER\-GUI 1 "2026-07-22" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-discover\-gui \- graphical browser for discoverable Mu2e DAQ resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-discover\-gui
.RB [ \-\-filter
.IR KEY=GLOB ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-retries
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-group
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR ip ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-auto ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-discover\-gui
multicasts the same DISCOVER query as
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
(protocol
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery/1 ,
group 239.255.42.99, UDP port 28999) and displays every ANNOUNCE reply
in a table.
.PP
The table shows all published parameters of each resource. The core
fields
.RB ( name ", " app ", " host ", " port ", " scheme ", " version ", "
.BR pid ", " started ", " id )
come first; any additional parameters a responder publishes in its
.B meta
map appear as further
.BI meta. key
columns, discovered at run time.
.PP
Rows are grouped by resource class: every instance that shares an
.B app
value is collected under a bold class row showing the instance count.
Classes can be expanded and collapsed individually or with the
.B Expand All
and
.B Collapse All
toolbar buttons.
.PP
Clicking a column header sorts by that field; clicking again reverses
the order.
.B port
and
.B pid
sort numerically, everything else sorts case\-insensitively as text.
Sorting applies to the class rows and to the instances within each
class. Column order can be rearranged by dragging headers.
.PP
Resources that advertise the same
.IR host : port
pair are treated as a conflict and drawn in bold red, with a tooltip
naming the contested endpoint. The status bar reports how many
conflicts were flagged.
.PP
If no resource replies, the table shows a single
.B "No resources found"
row and the status bar names the group and port that were probed.
.SH CONTEXT MENU
Right\-clicking a resource row offers:
.TP
.B Copy Record (Plain Text)
The whole record as aligned
.RI "" field " : " value
lines.
.TP
.B Copy Record (JSON)
The whole record as indented JSON, exactly as it came off the wire.
.TP
.BI "Copy \(dq" field "\(dq"
The value of the single field under the cursor.
.TP
.B Copy Field
A submenu with every published field of that record; choosing one
copies just that value.
.PP
Right\-clicking a class row instead offers
.B Copy Class (Plain Text)
and
.BR "Copy Class (JSON)" ,
covering every instance of that class.
.B Copy All Resources
(text or JSON) and
.B Probe Again
are always available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " KEY=GLOB"
Pre\-fill the toolbar filter. Keys:
.BR app ", " name ", " host .
Values are fnmatch\-style globs (e.g.\&
.BR app=vnc ).
The filter can be changed in the window at any time; press Enter to
re\-probe.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
How long each probe waits for replies. Default 2.0.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " n"
Number of query transmissions per probe. Default 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-group " addr"
Multicast group. Default 239.255.42.99.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
UDP port. Default 28999.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " ip"
Local interface address to send the multicast from. Useful on
multi\-homed DAQ nodes.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " seconds"
Auto\-probe interval. Default 10.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Start with auto\-probing enabled (equivalent to ticking
.B Auto
in the toolbar).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
YAML configuration file; see
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1).
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B F5
Probe now.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Precedence: command line > environment > config file > built\-in
defaults. Environment variables:
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_GROUP ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_PORT ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_INTERVAL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A Qt binding is required:
.B PyQt6
(preferred) or
.BR PySide6 .
Install with
.BR "pip install 'mu2edaq-discovery[gui]'" .
.SH NOTES
Multicast does not traverse the FNAL gateway. Run the GUI on a cluster
node (X11 forwarding or a VNC session) to see on\-site resources.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the Qt application exit code, 0 on a normal window close.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group.
